#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e83a5ba-83b1-5620-9b77-a5f9ceca89a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{b}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352295} {:answer/id #uuid "6f252992-bbb8-5043-9dda-2fb3232020cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352296} {:answer/id #uuid "160e7109-21ba-583a-bf44-dddea22b35d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352297} {:answer/id #uuid "3cbe346f-7894-54d3-afe6-23233fd890e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352298} {:answer/id #uuid "31500ce3-c0a2-5695-87c2-0cbd39a07e50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{b}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f252992-bbb8-5043-9dda-2fb3232020cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352296} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d012542-7176-595f-bd94-312364df2fb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "334676cf-0dd1-5735-bc6e-72eb49b9359e" :question/math-academy-id "q-170656" :question/problem "The bases of a trapezoid are increasing and the larger base is always twice the smaller base. The height of the trapezoid is $2\\,cm.$ Find the rate of change of the area of the trapezoid with respect to its smaller base $b.$" :question/worked-solution "The area of a trapezoid is given by \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{(B+b)h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is the smaller base, $B$ is the larger base and $h$ is the height of the trapezoid.\n\nWe are given that $B=2b$ and $h=2,$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the base $b$ by substituting $B=2b$ and $h=2$ in the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{(b+2b)(2)}{2}=3b.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(b)$ with respect to $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(b) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(3b) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(b) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1977d7ab-32a5-5fc2-9e99-bb39ba2991b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1977d7ab-32a5-5fc2-9e99-bb39ba2991b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352302} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a0248ff-1b8b-5b69-9237-e6c5c4d2985f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "750bc4e7-798f-5eba-ad9f-61537ac1f813" :question/math-academy-id "q-343169" :question/problem "Air is pumped into and released from a pressurized chamber. After $t$ minutes, the volume of air (in cubic meters) is modeled by\n\n$$\nA(t)=-6{t}^{2}+90t+400,\\,0\\le t\\le 15.\n$$\n\nFind the exact value of the instantaneous rate of change of the air volume with respect to time when $t=7$ minutes.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change when $t=7$ minutes is\n{{field-1}} cubic meters per minute." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the air volume at $t=7$ minutes is ${A}^{′}(7).$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{d}{dt}\\,(-6{t}^{2}+90t+400) \\\\  & =-12t+90.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=7,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(7) & =-12(7)+90 \\\\  & =-84+90 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the air volume at $t=7$ minutes is $6$ cubic meters per minute."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b4fd285-19ee-5346-a08a-1a8483262811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352305} {:answer/id #uuid "08961285-718b-541f-a56a-3caea667241f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08961285-718b-541f-a56a-3caea667241f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352306} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5419fb-8feb-57fd-b6a6-8e84ce71fbab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42884ae8-06df-563a-81bb-8d8c47e48c56" :question/math-academy-id "q-343404" :question/problem "The depth $D,$ in meters, of a plant’s root system after $t$ months is modeled by $D(t)=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{2t+13}.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the root depth when $t=6$ months?\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change when $t=6$ months is\n{{field-1}} meters per month." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the root depth when $t=6$ months is equal to ${D}^{′}(6).$ \n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{2t+13}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2t+13)^{(1/2)-1}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(2t+13)^{-1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{′}(6) & =\\frac{1}{4}(2(6)+13)^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the root depth when $t=6$ months is $\\frac{1}{20}$ meters per month."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217b3cdf-d9a6-5d92-af20-1a2fc17eaac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "217b3cdf-d9a6-5d92-af20-1a2fc17eaac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260015} :answer-field/id #uuid "9addb752-1c9d-5aa6-8cbb-442afe3f39ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a48171a-86f8-5d26-b8a7-cb6fe266dbbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-343499" :question/problem "The surface area $A$ of a cube is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the surface area of the cube is changing with respect to its side length at the moment when the side length of the cube is equal to $3\\,\\text{in}.$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at the moment when its side length is $3$ inches is equal to\n{{field-1}} ${\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{in}.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the surface area of a cube with side length $s$ is given by \n\n$$\nA=A(s)=6{s}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $A(s)$ with respect to $s$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(6{s}^{2}) \\\\  & =6(2s) \\\\  & =12s,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $s=3$ gives\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(3)=12(3)=36.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the surface area of the cube is changing when its side length is $3\\,\\text{in}$, is $36$ ${\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{in}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f768e2d-a1e8-56c7-a93c-031601a54e07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2l" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352309} {:answer/id #uuid "af472d1f-97c9-5a79-bc15-1a6b1670675b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "l" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352310} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0e5dd0-370a-5029-bd3a-8602ec423e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{l}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352311} {:answer/id #uuid "ececdeec-8160-5276-9f68-f0e0d45450c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{l}^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352312} {:answer/id #uuid "dd867a6a-4d54-5c05-81a2-d9e7c961c291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{l}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f768e2d-a1e8-56c7-a93c-031601a54e07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2l" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352309} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d013116-27c0-5024-a993-b98b4219b78b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "062fcd02-d338-5b14-8c30-fb2aac436416" :question/math-academy-id "q-48719" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066378/assets/2b5d589462bf2477be3d305ea88f3d5462b7d6ea4e001a9a71790d53e1683665.png)\n\nThe area of the square above is increasing. The length of the side of the square is $l.$ Find the rate of change of the area of a square with respect to the length of its side." :question/worked-solution "The area of the square is given by \n\n$$\nA=A(l)={l}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length of the side of the square.\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(l)$ with respect to $l$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(l) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}l}({l}^{2})=2l.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
